From: hjviewer <haejin.cho@yonsei.ac.kr>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 03:22:41 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 105/148] hjviewer: the PC locks again at a session's end if it
 was locked at its start (TV-W3)

TV-W3, PC side and proto (design build/v19/design/w3-w4.md 3-1, 5-1,
5-2; decisions D-9 and D-10; critic 2-3). New child module
src/server/connection/hjv_end_lock.rs; connection.rs gets thin hooks
only (a field, the logon response's platform_additions, update_options,
the on_close condition, the option classification).

- Proto: OptionMessage.hjv_end_lock = 1001 (HjvEndLock: UNSET, AUTO,
  ALWAYS, NEVER), additive. Classified as remote-screen only: a camera
  or terminal login drops it, an open session of another kind treats it
  as out of scope, and it is no part of the decoding-only no-op.
- Mode: the new field once sent, else the upstream field's explicit
  Yes (always) / No (never), else automatic for a same-account session,
  1.8.x controllers too (D-9). The upstream value a view-only switch
  sends with disable_keyboard is no lock choice (it would turn the
  automatic lock into never).
- Start: when the logon response of a pinned build's remote screen
  session is built (after the one proof record, critic 2-3), the PC
  reads is_prelogin || is_locked || is_logon_ui and keeps it per session
  key in memory, while a connection of the session holds it and ten
  minutes after; a reconnect inherits it (either locked = locked), a
  judged end forgets it.
- End: upstream's conditions stay (lock end, keyboard, not replaced by a
  reconnect); forced (TV-W5's cut, now EndLock::force) and always lock,
  never does not, automatic locks only if locked at the start and no
  other remote screen session is left. One log line per lock, no IDs.
  Unpinned builds lock exactly as upstream.
- Lock mark: a same-account session's PeerInfo.platform_additions gets
  hjv_end_lock {"v":1,"locked":...}; the controller shows the own-PC
  menu, the per-PC hide switch (D-10) and the close button's lock from
  it (controller step).
- hjv-e2e: HJV_E2E_LOGON=1 on the PC reads every start as locked and
  logs the lock instead of locking.

Tests: the decision table with upstream's conditions, unpinned and
non-remote sessions as upstream, the mode order, the view-only switch,
the start book (inherit, ten minutes, forget), the field's
classification.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
